This talk addresses the question of how empowerment (and lack thereof)
influences teaching and learning \LaTeX{}, on the example of creating
collaborative solutions between Humanities scholars and \LaTeX{}
consultants. It recounts the backstory behind the personas of Noob and
Ninja. It teaches four lessons on empowerment in teaching \LaTeX{}:

\begin{enumerate}
\raggedright
\item
  Empowerment is much more than providing motivation
\item
  Being welcoming
\item
  Focusing on teaching the basics extremely well
\item
  Empowering new users to find their own solutions
\end{enumerate}
